-- title:
--   Range of the abelian-quotient maps is the m-torsion
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $p$ prime and $p \nmid N_0$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$ (the hypothesis `A.LiesOverPrime p`). Let $\Lambda$ be a level datum for $(N_0,p,A)$ — a structure morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb Q$ localised at $p$ with $\sigma_A$ precomposed by the generic point equal to `genPt p`, a scheme $X$ over that base with a relative group law, a bijection $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$ from $J_0(N_0) = \operatorname{Pic}^0$ of the level-$N_0$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ onto the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points of $X$, and a bijection $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ from the corresponding Picard group over the residue field of $A$ onto the special-fibre points — satisfying `IsJacobian` (abelian-scheme properties, commutativity, additivity and Galois-equivariance of $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$, additivity of $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$, agreement of reduction with $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$, and existence of Hecke endomorphisms). Let $\mathcal O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` for these data, i.e. a smooth separated surjective group scheme $\mathcal O.g$ over the base with preconnected fibres, with a relative commutative group law, an additive Galois-equivariant parametrisation of $J_0(N_0p)$ by its generic points, Hecke endomorphisms, flat surjective multiplication-by-$n$ maps, proper generic fibre, a toric rank and abelian-quotient data on the special fibre. Let $\mathrm{abq}$ assign to each $m$ coprime to $p$ an additive map from $\mathcal O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ — the subgroup of $J_0(N_0p)$ generated by the $m$-torsion points whose associated generic point of $\mathcal O.g$ extends to an $A$-point — into $J_0(N_0) \times J_0(N_0)$, such that every value is killed by $m$, and such that for all such $m$, all $x \in \mathcal O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ and every $A$-point $s$ of $\mathcal O.g$ whose composite with $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ is the generic point attached to $x$, the reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ of the $i$-th component of $\mathrm{abq}_m(x)$ equals $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1}$ applied to the image of $s$ reduced to the residue field under the fibre map of $\mathcal O.\mathrm{abqFibre}\,i$, for $i = 0,1$. Then for every $m$ coprime to $p$ the range of $\mathrm{abq}_m$ is exactly the $m$-torsion subgroup of $J_0(N_0) \times J_0(N_0)$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of the description of the abelian quotient of the special fibre of the Néron model of $J_0(N_0p)$ at $p$, in the form used to compare $m$-torsion of $J_0(N_0p)$ with $m$-torsion of $J_0(N_0)^2$ in level lowering. It is characterised purely by the reduction formula, so it applies to any family of maps satisfying that formula, and it feeds the construction of such a family in `exists_abq_family_of_coprime`.
